{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/58369-i-m-curious-about-your-interest-in-kickstarter-highest-reward-levels","id":58369,"title":"I'm curious about your interest in Kickstarter highest reward levels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T15:40:38-08:00","id":58369,"title":"I'm curious about your interest in Kickstarter highest reward levels","content":"I understand that any Aeon/ Trinity Kickstarters if they happen are way off and may not follow the format of what has been done already as OPP evolves the Kickstarters necessarily as they go. However, I'm curious on your thoughts of the higher level reward tiers in OPP Kickstarters.<br /> <br /> I was skimming through the list of OPP Kickstarters and noticed that the highest level rewards are pretty much left unsold. Out of the 9 KS's I think OPP has done the highest level has been sold on only two of them - and I <i>think </i>I remember hearing that one of those was one of those annoying scam purchases.<br /> <br /> Although the details have evolved over the 9 KS's, generally you get a mix of the core deluxe edition, crediting in the book, wallpaper, perhaps a screen, some other PDFs, recently a discount on POD versions, inclusion in the development process in some way, and usually a game session run by the developer in person or online - for a price of between $2k to $3k or so.<br /> <br /> Looking at these I personally prefer actual non-digital product over, say, a game session run by the dev or inclusion in the design process in some way. So, while I could spring for the higher tier to support my fave game it'd be hard to justify as I can probably get all that really interests me at a much, much lower priced tier. But, I know I could be tempted to shell out more.<br /> <br /> So now I'm curious what others think of what's on offer in those highest reward tiers. <br /> <br /> What would it take to make you take the plunge? Are the actual items in the highest level reward level you've seen on the 9 Kickstarters appealing to you? Is the price too high to justify? Are you planning on going for it anyway?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:30:15-08:00","id":59143,"title":"","content":"I'm not likely to ever drop a few thou for people to storytell for me. I appreciate that there's more involved, supporting the product and the company, though.<br /> <br /> That said, I can appreciate why others might not want to throw in a lot of cash for the pdfs, when they have been readily, if illegally, available for years. Though I'm not sure how getting the pdfs like that would react with the PoD system, and whether you'd get cash off when purchasing them print on demand. That would certainly add some incentive to those levels.<br /> <br /> Obviously it would be great if we could get some solid books, but I get the feeling that they don't really have warehouses full of old books sitting anymore. So there's not much use thinking about it.<br /> <br /> The most tempting levels, to me, have been the ones that offer specialized aspects to the book, which is ridiculous, I know, but Anarchs Unbound in leather, Exalted in 'orichalcum' and so forth are nice ways to show some specialized interest in the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:02:18-08:00","id":59414,"title":"","content":"Good point nofather, I'd somehow forgotten about the super-special-versions in the kickstarters to date (i.e. Exalted orichalcum). There's an idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/58369-i-m-curious-about-your-interest-in-kickstarter-highest-reward-levels?p=59143#post59143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not likely to ever drop a few thou for people to storytell for me. I appreciate that there's more involved, supporting the product and the company, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same thoughts here. While I could stretch to the highest levels shown so far as a one off, the rewards just don't do it for me enough to justify it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/58369-i-m-curious-about-your-interest-in-kickstarter-highest-reward-levels?p=59143#post59143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I can appreciate why others might not want to throw in a lot of cash for the pdfs, when they have been readily, if illegally, available for years. Though I'm not sure how getting the pdfs like that would react with the PoD system, and whether you'd get cash off when purchasing them print on demand. That would certainly add some incentive to those levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm a bit of an idealist on this, but I really hate it when people suggest grabbing pirated PDFs of OPP / WW stuff. Its not like the price is insane for them on DTRPG. I get that for some, spending any money on gaming is tough due to personal circumstances and all, but it still bugs me as the industry isn't exactly flush with cash. I'm not suggesting you were advocating this, its just a pet peeve.<br /> <br /> Some of the rewards offered discounted PoD versions (&quot;close to cost as possible&quot; IIRC). So that's an incentive that could be interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/58369-i-m-curious-about-your-interest-in-kickstarter-highest-reward-levels?p=59143#post59143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously it would be great if we could get some solid books, but I get the feeling that they don't really have warehouses full of old books sitting anymore. So there's not much use thinking about it. <br /> <br /> The most tempting levels, to me, have been the ones that offer specialized aspects to the book, which is ridiculous, I know, but Anarchs Unbound in leather, Exalted in 'orichalcum' and so forth are nice ways to show some specialized interest in the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure. Warehouses of...well, anything really, are very much old model WW. And that makes perfect sense. I guess again for a couple grand I just feel something tangible would convince me, and digital products and a developer run game just don't come to that kinda cash level in my mind. But, springing for a high price tier plus adding to that a super-special-deluxe version ala Exalted or Anarchs could be the way to go. I'd definitely stick down cash for those, even if its not offering the level of support financially in the range of the highest price tier.<br /> <br /> Here's a few ideas that come to mind for the highest tier / as add-ons off the top of my head. No idea how feasible any of these are at all, and in all likelihood they aren't for various logistics / cost reasons:<ul><li>\u200bSome kind of subscription deal: Drop a couple of grand and get a PoD voucher every time a new book is released</li> <li>'Exclusive' content PDF / PoD: Get a limited run mini supplement not otherwise available (bet the price could go up for this actually) or...</li> <li>Early access content PDF / PoD: Get access to a mini supplement a good while before its made available to the public</li> </ul>Yeah....need to think more.<br /> <br /> Guess I'm just a sucker* for Trinity related 'stuff' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>*I went and bought a bunch of the original Trinity art and have that hanging in the man-cave. Whu? Obsessed, moi?</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:49:57-08:00","id":59453,"title":"","content":"*sob* I had a huge post written! With examples! Then I closed the tab by mistake. DAGNAMBIT!!!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was going to suggest that you may look into low-run custom game materials or art to encourage high-level backing? Who wouldn't want to rock an Orgotek shirt, or wear a &quot;Remember the Chibs&quot; armband? Functional stuff like shirts, pins, custom dice, special limited-edition ST screens or posters would be awesome stuff to have as high-level backer rewards.<br /> <br /> Fancy Dice? <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/waysidecreations/legend-of-grimrock-the-series/posts/720093\" target=\"_blank\">Check out this set of custom wooden d6's that the Legends of Grimrock kickstarter is offering for their backers.</a> Wooden might not be the way to go, but custom polymer <i>or metal!!</i> would be pretty awesome too. Trinity already has a signature font, that weird pseudo-Chinese stuff on the edges of a lot of illustrations. Even custom <i>dice-bags</i> would be pretty fun.<br /> <br /> Cool posters? Maybe some <a href=\"http://youngjerks.com/#/good-magazine/\" target=\"_blank\">Psi-Order recruitment posters</a>, <a href=\"http://www.topatoco.com/merchant.mvc?Screen=PROD&amp;Store_Code=TO&amp;Product_Code=DC-AWARENESS-PRINTS-S03&amp;Category_Code=DC-PRINTS\" target=\"_blank\">Anti-Aberrant PSAs</a> or <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Serenity-5-Piece-Travel-Poster-Series/dp/B000WWV4AQ\" target=\"_blank\">in-universe exotic locales</a>?<br /> <br /> Pretty much all the Psi Order logos are cool enough to go on stickers, pins or shirts. I'm personally a huge fan of the Chitra Bhanu and Orgotek logos. One of my geeky goals is to get a T-shirt from each of the major fictional MegaCorps (so far I have Weyland-Yutani and Blue Sun, waiting for a good Cyberdyne and/or Tyrell design) so I may be biased here. <br /> <br /> Books are great and all, but geeks and gamers get <i>serious</i> about our swag. We love to show off our hobbies, and physical merchandise is a pretty great way to do that <i>functionally</i> instead of just with prints and posters. I say this as a photographer and graphic designer, where all my personal art is non-functional. I <i>lurve</i> me some functional art and generally find myself much more willing to shell out for an awesome t-shirt as opposed to an awesome poster. I only have so many walls, you know? Bookshelves take up a lot of area!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T12:51:34-08:00","id":61003,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely love some of that merch, but I'm sure there are issues with doing that - stock, other logistics etc. Which is a shame. Because, shut up and take my money <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:29:48-08:00","id":61064,"title":"","content":"There are issues, Jeebus knows the Artisan Dice guys did a Kickstarter last year and their materials due to be delivered in M<i>ay</i> of last year were still being delivered in <i>January</i> of <i>this</i> year. However, Kickstarter backers tend to understand stuff like that and theirs is kind of an extreme case from what I've seen around Kickstarter. High-level backers tend to be few in number, meaning you can do low-run and keep the stock pretty small. There isn't much holding of stock since you can place the order once the Kickstarter succeeds, then receive and ship out the items as soon as they're produced, with minimal holding between receiving and shipping. Maybe you can talk to some other Kickstarter-ers that've done that? Like the Grimrock folks and the Artisan Dice guys, for example.<br /> <br /> Depending on what companies or artists you deal with to make the prints/posters/shirts/dice/beer-coozies, they might be really happy to work with you on logistics. Especially smaller artists that are interested in working on an RPG project, or might love the Trinityverse already. Just some brainings to cogitate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:10:34-08:00","id":62587,"title":"","content":"Interesting to hear about experiences with Artisan Dice. <br /> <br /> I think, and I'm just guessing, that greater ranges of merchandise (other than the deluxes themselves or PoD from DTRPG) might be a bit of a distraction from where energy is being spent right now - not to mention new logistical challenges. OPP readily acknowledges that it is still evolving how this all works for them so it'll take time to figure out what works best. <br /> <br /> Would I stick some money down for more interesting merchandise though, heck yes. Perhaps by the end of the year, or whenever the Trinity KS's get going things will have moved on more to allow this. That's two of us at least that could be persuaded to part with more money for more 'stuff' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T19:39:30-08:00","id":63246,"title":"","content":"I would love if they did dice sets as kick starter rewards. also, I'd love a &quot;I'm Mal'icious&quot; T-shirt, as well as a couple of T2M logos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:55:39-08:00","id":64619,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm Divis Malicious&quot; would be even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:32:34-08:00","id":65012,"title":"","content":"&quot;Divis Mal has arms?!?&quot; HAS to go on a shirt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Heh, I <i>still</i> have my old and heavily worn Orgotek t-shirt. Granted, its damn near falling to pieces now and...um....well, I was thinner way back when I bought it, ahem. My Strike Team Psion shirt is in really good condition, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T19:09:44-08:00","id":65305,"title":"","content":"I have always been fond of collector pins. A small set of symbol pins would be pretty cool KS collectable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T05:12:25-08:00","id":65573,"title":"","content":"I have the original Trinity collector pin. I would love if they remade the old Trinity dice. Its the only thing I don't have from the original set.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://s1345.photobucket.com/user/karpomatic/media/pic831685_t_zpsf9b8a376.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1345.photobucket.com/albums/p665/karpomatic/pic831685_t_zpsf9b8a376.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T16:27:49-08:00","id":66048,"title":"","content":"Reignhell, karpomatic - those dice and pins were great (still have mine actually).<br /> <br /> What about at the highest level of reward? Any thoughts on what would tempt you at those levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T16:49:05-08:00","id":66072,"title":"","content":"Hmm..<br /> <br /> 1) Ultra-Rare Editions: Much like the Exalted &quot;Oricalcum&quot; Edition or the Werewolf &quot;Metal&quot; Edition, a made to order print run of a Aeon &quot;Olaminium&quot; edition would be pretty cool.<br /> 2) Contributing: Being able to contribute to the setting, even if you just get to sit in on the developers conversations, would be a thrill. I enjoy the process of world building and setting design, and being able to add some bit of official content to the setting could be a good high-tier reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T20:01:45-08:00","id":66215,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of contributing. Writing an in-character section, maybe? With the understanding that it'd have to meet guide-lines and be edited. Trinity and Aberrant were full of little in-character snippits like emails and interviews. It'd be fun to write some of those!<br /> <br /> Or get to design a signature character? Also fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T08:57:34-08:00","id":66521,"title":"","content":"I would be super interested in a backer level that let me create my own signature character that would be included in the book. I'm all in for that for Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T17:15:46-08:00","id":68155,"title":"","content":"Backer contributions could be fun actually..... Meeting various standards though obviously, with OPP having final say on what's acceptable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T18:17:33-08:00","id":70206,"title":"","content":"Getting to actually write a section might be somewhat unlikely, bu